          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            An (oriented)
            %em cobordism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            from an (oriented)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi in
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{in}
            to an (oriented) smooth manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi out
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{out}
            is a smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold+with+boundary"} manifold with boundary
            such that its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary"} boundary
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∂
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi in
                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi out
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\partial \Sigma \simeq X_{in} \coprod X_{out}
          %p
            with induced
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation"} orientation
            agreeing with the given one on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi in
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{in}
            and being the opposite of that of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi out
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{out}
            (
            %a{:href => "#Thom54"}> Thom 54, Chapter IV, p. 64
            ). Hence by labelling disjoint components of the boundary of any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold+with+boundary"} manifold with boundary
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            as either “incoming” or “outgoing”, then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            becomes a cobordism from its incoming to its outgoing boundary components.
          %p
            (While
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi in
                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi out
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{in} \coprod X_{out}
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary"} boundary
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            is the “co-boundary” of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi in
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi out
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{in}\coprod X_{out}
            = succeed "." do
              %em bordism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bordism+homology+theory"} bordism homology theory
            and
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+cohomology+theory"} cobordism cohomology theory
          %p
            With a few technical conditions on the boundary inclusions added, then
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism"} diffeomorphism
            classes of
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            (a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+cobordisms"} category of cobordisms
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            are the manifolds, whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            are the cobordisms, and whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
            operation is the operation of gluing two cobordisms along a common boundary component. Such a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+cobordisms"} category of cobordisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Bord
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Bord_n
            of some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            is naturally a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Bord
                    %mi n
                    %mo ⊔
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Bord_n^{\sqcup}
            with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            being the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊔
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sqcup
            of manifolds.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+components"} connected components
            in this category are called
            %em cobordism classes
            of manifolds. Under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+product"} cartesian product
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+ring"} cobordism ring
            in the given dimension. The study of these classes, hence of manifolds “up to cobordisms”, is a central topic in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+topology"} algebraic topology
          %p
            A central insight connecting
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+topology"} algebraic topology
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematical+physics"} mathematical physics
            is that a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monoidal+functor"} strong monoidal functor
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+cobordisms"} category of cobordisms
            with values in something like the category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vect"} Vect
            (with its standard
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+modules"} tensor product of modules
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            is called a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+quantum+field+theory"} topological quantum field theory
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Z
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Bord
                    %mi n
                    %mo ⊔
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msup
                    %mi Vect
                    %mo ⊗
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Z \colon Bord_n^\sqcup \longrightarrow Vect^\otimes
                  \\,.
          %p
            Here one thinks of a cobordism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            as a piece of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            (or
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
            (or
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane"} brane
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
            as above is then thought of as sending each
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+quantum+states"} space of quantum states
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z(X)
            and each spacetime
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            between
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi in
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{in}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi out
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{out}
            to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+map"} linear map
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi in
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi out
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z(\Sigma)\colon Z(X_{in}) \longrightarrow Z(X_{out})
          %p
            From the perspective of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematics"} mathematics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism"} diffeomorphism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariants"} invariants
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+manifolds"} closed manifolds
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            into pieces and being able to reconstruct them from gluing of data associated to manifolds with
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
          %p
            If one considers
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds+with+corners"} manifolds with corners
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+cobordisms"} extended cobordisms
            of any dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            going between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+cobordisms"} extended cobordisms
            of dimension
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k-1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            form a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28infinity%2Cn%29-category"} symmetric monoidal (infinity,n)-category
            called, naturally, the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2Cn%29-category+of+cobordisms"} (infinity,n)-category of cobordisms
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+hypothesis"} cobordism hypothesis
            asserts that this is a most fundamental object in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+algebra"} higher algebra
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+construction"} free
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28infinity%2Cn%29-category"} symmetric monoidal (infinity,n)-category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2Cn%29-category+with+duals"} with duals
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+quantum+field+theory"} topological quantum field theory
            is accordingly called
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+TQFT"} extended TQFT
            or similar.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#RelationToCohomotopy Relation to Cohomotopy
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontrjagin-Thom+isomorphism"} Pontrjagin-Thom isomorphism
            says that assigning
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cohomotopy+charge"} Cohomotopy charge
            identifies suitable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+classes"} cobordism classes
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submanifolds"} submanifolds
            or abstract
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds"} manifolds
            with
